Purpose: 
Lambda needs permission to interact with other AWS services. Instead of giving permissions directly to the Lambda, we give it an IAM execution role.
We attached:
AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole- This allows Lambda to write its execution logs to CloudWatch.

Go to:
AWS Console → Lambda → Functions → Create function
Choose:
- Author from scratch
- Function name: InterviewLambda
- Runtime: Node.js 22.x
- Architecture: x86_64
- Permissions → Use an existing role
- Existing role: InterviewLambdaRole

Click Create function
